From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:16:28 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: cpif: pktproc: allow an uncached link without IO
 coherency

The packet processor refused any device tree whose
pktproc_dl_use_hw_iocc differed from CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC, and
that option is always on. zumapro's modem link turns IO coherency on
only when the device tree gives it samsung,sysreg, which the Pixel 9a's
doesn't yet, so its cpif node says use_hw_iocc 0 with every region
uncached, as the 9a's bring-up stack runs it (CP ONLINE and thousands of
link cycles, with cpif built without LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC). The
in-tree cpif refused that node:

  cpif: pktproc_get_info: iocc:0 max_packet_size:1584 baaw:0
  cpif: pktproc_get_info: PCIe IOCC config and dt are inconsistent

What the option decides is whether the software cache maintenance for a
cached downlink buffer region is built. A link without IO coherency
needs it only when that region is cached, so refuse just that case, and
keep refusing use_hw_iocc 1 without the option. The uplink has no such
maintenance in either build, so refuse its cached regions without IO
coherency whatever the option, not only when it is off.

gs201's device tree (use_hw_iocc 1, regions cached) passes as before.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/Kconfig           |  5 ++++-
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_rx_pktproc.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_tx_pktproc.c |  3 +--
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/Kconfig
index 6c618fa9c..c0209f8c0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/Kconfig
@@ -57,7 +57,10 @@ config LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC
 	  The gs201 modem link driver turns IO coherency on for the link at
 	  every link-up, before the modem may DMA, so the packet processor
 	  treats its cacheable regions as coherent, as stock does
-	  (pantah_defconfig: CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC=y).
+	  (pantah_defconfig: CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC=y). On zumapro it
+	  does so only when the device tree gives it samsung,sysreg; a link
+	  without it sets pktproc_dl_use_hw_iocc and pktproc_ul_use_hw_iocc
+	  to 0 and keeps the packet processor's regions uncached.
 
 config CP_PKTPROC
 	bool "Packet processor, downlink (bring-up)"
diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_rx_pktproc.c b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_rx_pktproc.c
index 9581e13bb..ebaf595e1 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_rx_pktproc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_rx_pktproc.c
@@ -1816,11 +1816,23 @@ static int pktproc_get_info(struct pktproc_adaptor *ppa, struct device_node *np)
 	}
 #endif
 
-	/* Check if config and dt are consistent */
-	if (ppa->use_hw_iocc != IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC)) {
+	/*
+	 * Check if config and dt are consistent. A link without IO coherency
+	 * (zumapro's without samsung,sysreg) says use_hw_iocc 0, and is fine
+	 * as long as its buffers are uncached: the cache maintenance that
+	 * cached buffers would need is built only without
+	 * LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC. pktproc_create() refuses cached info and
+	 * descriptor regions without IO coherency either way.
+	 */
+	if (ppa->use_hw_iocc && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC)) {
 		mif_err("PCIe IOCC config and dt are inconsistent\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
+	if (!ppa->use_hw_iocc && ppa->buff_rgn_cached &&
+	    IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC)) {
+		mif_err("cached buffers without IOCC need LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC off\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	pktproc_adjust_size(ppa);
 
diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_tx_pktproc.c b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_tx_pktproc.c
index 5cef06197..a04f982ed 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_tx_pktproc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/link_tx_pktproc.c
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@ int pktproc_create_ul(struct platform_device *pdev, struct mem_link_device *mld,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-#if !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LINK_DEVICE_PCIE_IOCC)
+	/* The uplink has no cache maintenance, whatever the config */
 	if (!ppa_ul->use_hw_iocc && ppa_ul->info_rgn_cached) {
 		mif_err("cannot support sw iocc based caching on info region\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -437,7 +437,6 @@ int pktproc_create_ul(struct platform_device *pdev, struct mem_link_device *mld,
 		mif_err("cannot support sw iocc based caching on buff region\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-#endif
 
 	/* Get base addr */
 	mif_info("memaddr:0x%lx memsize:0x%08x\n", memaddr, memsize);
